@@ -0,0 +1,175 @@
+# SpiderMonkey JIT backend for 32-bit PowerPC (JS_CODEGEN_PPC)
+
+Target: PowerBook G4, MPC7447A (G4, "7450 family"), 32-bit big-endian,
+Linux, SysV PPC32 ABI (secure-PLT), Arch POWER `powerpc`.
+Tree: op64k `~/Projects/firefox-ppc32/src/firefox-154.0.1`, git branch `ppc32-jit`.
+Backend dir: `js/src/jit/ppc/`. It started as a mechanical copy of the ppc64
+backend (`js/src/jit/ppc64/`, from Arch POWER's 0004/0005 patches, POWER8+,
+ELFv2, PUNBOX64, VSX, wasm) with `ppc64`->`ppc` renamed. It must become a
+32-bit, NUNBOX32, pre-VSX, no-wasm backend.
+
+Reference backends:
+- `jit/ppc64/` - PowerPC idioms: LR/CTR calls, CR-based branches, patchable
+  jumps, frame layout with LR as an SPR, icache flushing. Keep these.
+- `jit/arm/` - the only surviving 32-bit NUNBOX32 backend: ValueOperand as
+  (type, payload) register pairs, Register64 as (high, low) pairs, the
+  32-bit versions of every MacroAssembler method (`DEFINED_ON(... arm ...)`
+  lists in `jit/MacroAssembler.h` now all include `ppc` too). When unsure
+  what a method must do on 32-bit, copy ARM's semantics, emit PPC instrs.
+- `jit/x86/` - the other 32-bit NUNBOX32 backend (Value/int64 pair logic).
+
+## Scope
+
+- Baseline interpreter, Baseline JIT, CacheIR ICs, Ion (Warp), irregexp
+  native regexps. These are what make the browser fast.
+- **No wasm.** `wasm::HasPlatformSupport()` returns false on ppc32. Wasm-only
+  MacroAssembler methods and wasm LIR/codegen: `MOZ_CRASH("ppc32: no wasm")`.
+- **No SIMD.** Delete every Simd128 / VSX / VMX code path; methods that are
+  SIMD-only are not DEFINED_ON ppc anyway (lists without `arm`).
+- Must compile warning-clean enough for `-Werror`-free build (not required
+  to be warning free) and pass `config/check_macroassembler_style.py`
+  (runs at the end of the JS shell build).
+
+## ISA: what a 7447A has (and has NOT)
+
+Only emit instructions from the 32-bit PowerPC UISA + AltiVec-era CPU:
+
+ALLOWED: add addc adde addze addme addi addis addic addic. subf subfc subfe
+subfze subfme subfic neg mullw mulli mulhw mulhwu divw divwu (and the `o`
+/ `.` forms) and or xor nand nor eqv andc orc andi. andis. ori oris xori
+xoris slw srw sraw srawi rlwinm rlwnm rlwimi cntlzw extsb extsh cmpw cmpwi
+cmplw cmplwi (cmp/cmpl with L=0) lbz lbzx lbzu lhz lhzx lha lhax lwz lwzx
+lwzu lwzux stb stbx sth sthx stw stwx stwu stwux lmw stmw lhbrx lwbrx sthbrx
+stwbrx lwarx stwcx. sync isync eieio mfcr mtcrf mfspr mtspr (LR CTR XER)
+crand cror crxor crnor creqv crandc crorc mcrf mcrxr b bl bc bcl bclr bclrl
+bcctr bcctrl tw twi dcbf dcbst dcbz icbi
+FP: lfs lfsx lfsu lfd lfdx lfdu stfs stfsx stfd stfdx stfdu stfiwx fmr fneg
+fabs fnabs fadd(s) fsub(s) fmul(s) fdiv(s) fmadd(s) fmsub(s) fnmadd(s)
+fnmsub(s) frsp fctiw fctiwz fcmpu fcmpo fsel fres frsqrte mffs mtfsf mtfsfi
+mtfsb0 mtfsb1 mcrfs
+
+FORBIDDEN (SIGILL on the G4): anything doubleword: ld ldx ldu std stdx stdu
+lwa lwax rldic* rldimi rldcl rldcr sld srd srad sradi mulld mulhd mulhdu
+divd divdu cntlzd extsw ldarx stdcx. ldbrx stdbrx cmpd/cmpld (L=1); also
+isel, fsqrt fsqrts (the 7447A has NO hardware square root), fcfid fcfids
+fcfidu fctid fctidz fctiduz, fcpsgn, frim frip friz frin, lfiwax lfiwzx,
+popcntb popcntw popcntd, cnttzw cnttzd, cmpb, modsw moduw modsd modud,
+mfocrf/mtocrf (use mfcr/mtcrf), lbarx lharx stbcx. sthcx., setb setbc,
+darn, every VSX (x*) instruction, mtvsr*/mfvsr*, POWER9/10 anything.
+The Assembler will MOZ_CRASH/static-fail on forbidden emitters; do not call them.
+
+Replacement idioms:
+- GPR<->FPR moves go through memory: use a stack slot (e.g. `stwu`/stack
+  temp at -16(r1) below the red zone is NOT safe: ppc32 SysV has **no red
+  zone**, so reserve stack first) or a scratch area. Prefer reserving 16
+  bytes of stack (`stwu r1,-16(r1)` style via the MacroAssembler's
+  reserveStack/freeStack) around the move.
+- int32 -> double: the 0x43300000:0x80000000 magic-double trick
+  (store 0x43300000 / (x ^ 0x80000000) as a double, lfd, fsub the magic
+  constant 0x4330000080000000). uint32 -> double: same with payload x and
+  magic 0x4330000000000000.
+- double -> int32 (truncate): `fctiwz fX,fY; stfd fX,tmp; lwz rD,tmp+4`
+  (big-endian: low word at +4). Check for out-of-range/NaN as ARM/x86 do
+  (fctiwz saturates to 0x7fffffff/0x80000000; NaN -> 0x80000000).
+- sqrt: call the C library (`sqrt`/`sqrtf`) via an ABI call, like ARM
+  soft paths do, or use frsqrte + Newton only if exact (it is not: use libm).
+- floor/ceil/trunc/round: no fri*: either the fctiwz-based int32 paths
+  (branch to bailout/fail when out of int32 range, as the shared code
+  expects for `floorDoubleToInt32` etc.) or ABI calls to libm.
+- copysign: via memory (stfd, bit ops on the high word, lfd).
+- count trailing zeros: `cntlzw` on `(x & -x)` then `31 - n`.
+- popcount: the classic SWAR sequence (as ARM does).
+- 8/16-bit atomics: lwarx/stwcx. on the containing aligned word with
+  masking/shifting (big-endian lane positions!), like MIPS does.
+- 64-bit atomics: NOT available in hardware. Only wasm needs the masm
+  atomic64 ops; implement `MOZ_CRASH` and make sure CacheIR/Ion paths that
+  would need them are not taken (see `jit::AtomicOperations` / x86 which
+  uses cmpxchg8b; we cannot). BigInt64 Atomics then go through C++.
+- select/conditional move: branch around a `mr` (no isel).
+- Min/max double: compare+branch (no xsmaxjdp).
+
+## ABI (SysV PPC32, Linux)
+
+- GPRs 32-bit. r0 volatile (reads as 0 in RA of D-form loads/addi: never
+  use as a base). r1 = sp. **r2 = thread pointer (TLS): never write.**
+  **r13 = small-data anchor: never write.** r3-r10 args (volatile),
+  r11-r12 volatile scratch, r14-r31 callee-saved.
+- Return: int32/pointer in r3; int64 in r3 (high) : r4 (low);
+  double/float in f1.
+- 64-bit int args occupy an aligned pair r3:r4, r5:r6, r7:r8, r9:r10 (high
+  word in the lower-numbered register); if no pair is left they go on the
+  stack 8-byte aligned and no later int arg goes in registers.
+- FP args f1-f8 (floats also in FPRs); overflow on the stack (8-aligned).
+- f0-f13 volatile, f14-f31 callee-saved.
+- Stack: 16-byte aligned at calls. **No red zone.** Linkage area of the
+  caller is 8 bytes: 0(sp) = back chain, 4(sp) = where the *callee* saves
+  LR. Stack arguments start at 8(sp). So `ShadowStackSpace = 8` and the
+  ABIArgGenerator starts stack offsets at 8.
+- No TOC, no function descriptors (all the ppc64 `_CALL_ELF == 1` /
+  ELFv1 descriptor code is irrelevant: delete it).
+- LR is an SPR (not a GPR): JIT frames push the return address callee-side
+  (`JS_USE_LINK_REGISTER` is defined for PPC; `pushReturnAddress` =
+  `mflr r0; stwu/push r0`). Calls: `bl` for near labels, or
+  `lis/ori + mtctr + bctrl` for absolute/patchable targets.
+
+## Register assignment (keep the ppc64 names/choices where possible)
+
+- StackPointer r1, FramePointer r31, ReturnReg r3,
+  ReturnReg64 = Register64(r3 /*high*/, r4 /*low*/).
+- Non-allocatable: r0, r1, r2 (TLS), r11, r12 (scratch), r13 (SDA),
+  r16 (SavedScratchRegister), r31 (FP). Allocatable: the other 24.
+- JSReturnOperand = ValueOperand(JSReturnReg_Type = r6, JSReturnReg_Data = r5).
+- Float: FloatRegisters has only two kinds, Double (codes 0-31) and Single
+  (codes 32-63); `SetType = uint64_t`. f0 = ScratchDoubleReg/
+  ScratchFloat32Reg (non-allocatable). ReturnDoubleReg = f1.
+  All FPR pushes (PushRegsInMask, RegisterDump, bailouts) store **8-byte
+  doubles** (`stfd`), singles included (an FPR always holds double format;
+  shared code reads FLOAT32_REG as a double on PPC).
+- `ScalePointer = TimesFour`, `sizeof(void*) == 4`.
+
+## Value / int64 layout (big-endian!)
+
+- `JS::Value` is a uint64 `asBits_` with the tag in the high 32 bits. In
+  memory on big-endian the **tag is at offset 0 and the payload at offset 4**:
+  `NUNBOX32_TYPE_OFFSET = 0`, `NUNBOX32_PAYLOAD_OFFSET = 4`
+  (ARM/x86 are the opposite). Every `ToPayload(addr)` = addr+4,
+  `ToType(addr)` = addr+0. Doubles stored in a Value slot: `stfd`/`lfd` at
+  offset 0 (same bytes as the uint64 - natural on BE).
+- int64 in memory: high word at offset 0, low at 4:
+  `INT64HIGH_OFFSET = 0`, `INT64LOW_OFFSET = 4` (jit/Registers.h has an
+  `#if` for JS_CODEGEN_PPC). Use `HighWord()/LowWord()` helpers, never
+  hard-code 0/4 for int64 halves.
+- Moving a double between an FPR and a (type, payload) register pair:
+  stfd to a temp slot, lwz type from +0, lwz payload from +4 (and back).
+
+## Coding rules
+
+- Keep the ppc64 names of Assembler emitters that exist on the G4
+  (`as_lwz`, `as_stw`, `as_addi`, `as_rlwinm`, `xs_mtctr`, `xs_mflr`, ...).
+  `Assembler-ppc.h` (owned by the lead) is the single source of instruction
+  emitters; if you need one that is missing and legal, ask the lead via
+  your report or add it at the end of `Assembler-ppc.h` in the section
+  `// --- added by <agent> ---` (append-only, nothing else in that file).
+- Pointers are 32-bit: loadPtr = lwz, storePtr = stw, addPtr = add, etc.
+  Immediates: `li`/`lis+ori` (max 2 instructions for any 32-bit value).
+- Every ppc64 construct using doubleword instructions must be rewritten,
+  not wrapped. `grep -nE 'as_(ld|std|rld|sld|srd|srad|mulld|divd|extsw|cmpd|cmpld|isel|fsqrt|fcfid|fctid|fcpsgn|fri[mpzn]|popcnt|cnttz|mod|lfiw|x[sv]|mtvsr|mfvsr|ldarx|stdcx)'`
+  must come back empty in the ppc/ directory when you are done.
+- Unimplemented-but-reachable paths: `MOZ_CRASH("ppc32: <what>")`, never
+  silently wrong code. Wasm and SIMD: `MOZ_CRASH("ppc32: no wasm")`.
+- Comments: explain PPC32/BE specifics briefly; no history narration.
+- Do not edit shared (non-ppc/) files without saying so in your report;
+  the lead owns shared files, the build, and git commits. Do not commit.
+
+## Build / test (lead runs these; agents may compile-check)
+
+- JS shell mozconfig: `~/Projects/firefox-ppc32/mozconfig-js` (add
+  `--enable-jit` in place of `--disable-jit --enable-portable-baseline-interp`
+  once it compiles), objdir `src/obj-js-ppc32`.
+- Compile check a single unified TU: `cd src/obj-js-ppc32/js/src/jit && make <file>.o`
+  (see `backend.mk`/`Makefile` for the Unified_cpp_js_src_jit*.o names), or
+  `bash -c '. ~/Projects/firefox-ppc32/scripts/env.sh; MOZCONFIG=~/Projects/firefox-ppc32/mozconfig-js ./mach build -j40 js/src/jit'` style.
+- Run: `~/Projects/firefox-ppc32/scripts/js-qemu` (qemu-ppc -cpu 7447_v1.1
+  with the G4 sysroot) - SIGILL under qemu means a forbidden instruction.
+- jit-tests: `cd js/src/jit-test && python3 jit_test.py -j 150 --timeout 600 ~/Projects/firefox-ppc32/scripts/js-qemu <dir>`;
+  baseline (no-JIT) failures: `~/Projects/firefox-ppc32/jittest/baseline-nojit-basic.txt`.
